Served the Defendants
Provided urgent medical evidence
=20

3. Request for Immediate Action

=20

Given:
the medically urgent situation,
the ACO-compliant bundle now filed,
the fact that the N463 has been pending since 25 November,
and the statutory duties engaged,
=20

I respectfully request:

=20

(1) Sealing of the N461 today

=20

(2) Immediate referral of the N463 to a judge today

=20

(3) Confirmation of urgent listing

=20

I would be grateful for written confirmation of receipt, acceptance, and se=
aling.

=20

Thank you for your attention to this urgent and medically fragile matter.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

From: Administrative Court Office Immediates <administrativecourtoffice.imm=
ediates@justice.gov.uk>
Date: Friday, November 28, 2025 at 7:06=E2=80=AFAM
To: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>
Subject: Re: URGENT: Filing of N461 Judicial Review Bundle =E2=80=94 Request for =
Immediate Sealing & Judicial Consideration

=20

Good afternoon,

=20

Please note an ACO compliant bundle must be filed as soon as possible: Admi=
nistrative Court: Information for Court Users =E2=80=93 June 2022 - Courts and Tri=
bunals Judiciary

=20

Please see guidance attached https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/20=
22/07/Administrative-Court-Information-for-court-users-June22.pdf)

=20

The court cannot accept your application and supporting documents in separa=
ted documents and multiple emails.

=20

Please resubmit and ensure all key supporting documents are available for r=
eview.

=20

=20

Kind regards,

S Sikity**OFFICIAL**

Administrative Court Office | Issues and Enquiries

=20

King's Bench Division | HMCTS | Royal Courts of Justice| Strand, London | W=
C2A 2LL

Phone: 020 7947 6000

Web: www.gov.uk/hmcts

PLEASE DO NOT SEND EMAILS TO PERSONAL INBOXES AS NO ACTION WILL BE TAKEN. P=
ERSONAL INBOXES ARE NOT MONITORED. PLEASE SEND ALL EMAILS TO :

administrativecourtoffice.generaloffice@justice.gov.uk


Daily Cause List: http://www.justice.gov.uk/courts/court-lists/list-rcj
Listing Enquiries: listoffice@administrativecourtoffice.justice.gov.uk

General Enquiries: generaloffice@administrativecourtoffice.justice.gov.uk

Criminal & Extradition Enquiries: crimex@administrativecourtoffice.justice.=
gov.uk

Skeleton Arguments: london.skeletonarguments@administrativecourtoffice.just=
ice.gov.uk

=20

For information on how HMCTS uses personal data about you please see: https=
://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about=
/personal-information-charter

=20

In accordance with Practice Direction 5B - Electronic communication and fil=
ing we ask you to do the following when sending an e-mail message to the cou=
rt:
Clearly state the Court's action number, parties=E2=80=99 names and any dates rel=
ating to an up-coming hearing in the subject header.
In accordance with Practice Direction 3.3a, please do not submit documents =
which carry a payable fee; such e-mails will be deleted.
